at the  society that we live in like people to  be in bad debt  because then they have to rely on jobs  they have to rely on the government and  it just keeps but that that's my opinion  but looking at it from the lender's  perspective  if you're going in and you're getting a  personal loan if you've got bad  credit if you've got no job if you've  got  no means to not only pay the money back  but to even pay the interest payment  they're not going to want to give you  the money  and on top of that if you've got no  assets if you don't own anything  because if they give you 20 grand as a  loan but they know that you've got  your own home you're in a job your  wife's got a job and  nothing are you know what even if they  it has to kill them to pay the interest  we'll get it because if we don't get it  we'll go after them  for their house or whatever so they'll  give you the loan  you'll be a guarantor to the loan you'll  have to pay it back and that's that's a  personal loan i don't like personal  loans for those reasons  i think if you can't afford something  then just  don't get it you might be like i thought  samuel loved  debt different kind of debt so the next  kind of debt  is which is very very similar is a  residential  mortgage that is effectively  the same thing in a way as getting a  loan for  a wedding because if you're getting a  loan out for a house to live in  you're gonna have to pay that money back  you're gonna have to pay that money back  at some point  and how you're gonna pay back you're not  going to be able to rent the house out  you're not going to  so this is why i rent where i live  because again getting a loan out which a  mortgage by the way is a loan  getting a loan out to buy a house to  live in the house  is just basically buying something you  can't afford it  it's buying something that's not going  to give you any money back it's a  liability  so that's why they're so strict  on on mortgages if you're trying to get  a residential mortgage to live in  you need to prove so much they're going  to look at how much you earn  they're going to ask you how much you  spend they're going to ask you  if you've got any dependables and how  much that costs they're going to want to  know  your age they're going to look at your  salary your earnings  and they're going to really really go  through you with fine tooth game to  check  that you can get the mortgage and the  reason is is because they know that if  you buy a house to live in and you can't  pay the mortgage back  it's going to be a pain now of course  they're going to take the house off you  but they're going really really really  pre-qualify you before you move into a  house to live in  so that's personal loans that's a  personal mortgage to live in  kind of sometimes tough to get if you  want to get that kind of loan probably  shouldn't  then you need to have a good credit and  you need to have a decent income coming  in the more  the higher your income the better your  credit the easier you're going to be  able to get that kind of debt  and what a lot of middle class people do  is they get wrapped up  in personal debt because  they think oh i've got a good income  i've got a good credit  wow i can i can get 50 grand a loan well  personally 50 grand and every time you  go into the bank they'll say would you  like a loan would you like a loan  they'll almost press you to get a loan  they'll charge you a really high  interest  you think i'll get it because i can  you'll get it and then you just have to  work harder on your job  and then that's what we call the rat  race and you know they say even if you  win the rat race you're still a rat  so that is personal loans then we've got  business loans  now business loan as if maybe you know  you see on dragon's den where they'll be  pitching  the the the dragons that's not a  business loan because  that's a dragon putting money investing  money into the business  that's more like a joint venture  agreement um a  business loan would be when you go to a  bank and you say hey could i have  50 000 pounds as a startup loan and you  give back a fixed return  just to get your business started now  business loans historically are really  tough to get because in the same way  as a personal loan the lender the bank  needs to be able to know that the  business is going to be able to pay back  the money the business needs to be  strong enough it needs to have  be tried and tested but the thing is if  the business is  tried and tested is making good money  you probably don't need the business  loan in the first place  it's like a catch 22. now at the moment  they are giving bounce-back loans uh and  and the interest on these is absolutely  next to nothing  so i would probably suggest if you can  if you have  a a company set up you can apply  for a bounce back loan i'd probably  suggest i'd highly suggest at least  exploring that option because i can't  remember the top my head exactly what  the interest is i've done videos about  this before  but i took one i took a bounce back loan  so that's a business loan  for your business and it might have  strings attached  obviously if it's a business loan you  need to use it for your business  you can't take a business loan and then  go and holiday with it because that's  not  what the purpose of the loan is that's a  business loan  and then it brings us onto a completely  different type of bank loans and type of  debt  and this is when you're borrowing money  for  to invest it into an asset  completely different if you're borrowing  money from a bank  to buy a buy to let property the  criteria  the whole everything about it is  different  why is it different because instead of  you taking that money out  for yourself you're taking that money  out  to invest it into something that's going  to give you back money and you're going  gonna use that money  for yourself this is actually good debt  difference between bad debt and good  debt  so the great thing is you might think  i'd never be able to get a loan out  to invest in property my credit's not  very good  my salary is not very good i'm too young  i'm too  old i'm too this unto that but actually  if it's a buy to let mortgage  if it's a loan for investment purposes  well think of it from the lender's  perspective  do they care about you not really what  do they care about  they care about the money's going to be  able to pay back to them so therefore  they care about  where the money is going so what they do  with buy delay is they'll look at the  investment so they'll say oh you want to  borrow 100 grand to buy a house to rent  out  okay what's the house okay let's have a  look at the house  how much will that ran out for and  they'll check it out  hmm what's the value of it what have you  got a good deal on the house  they're looking at the investment not  the person that they're investing into  this is really good news by the way  because sometimes people say to me they  say samuel when when are the banks don't  stop giving you money to buy properties  and but  to buy houses you know is there only so  many mortgages that you can get  is there only so much that you can  borrow and the answer is not really no  there's not  you can borrow millions and millions and  millions and millions of pounds  but it's not personal debt  it's debt to invest it's good debt  so if you want to be able to start  getting uh buy to let mortgages  sure if you've got decent credit it  helps  you know if you've got a salary but i  know people that have got a 5 000 pound  salary  they make five grand a year and they're  getting by to let mortgages no problem  it also helps a little bit if you own a  residential property that is an  advantage to owning a residential  property because  they think oh well you've got a bit of  experience in property for some reason  but i didn't have a residential mortgage  i started in buy to let and i've now got  a  very very i have millions and millions  of pounds worth of debt  but it's good debt not bad debt so i  just thought i'd give because i get so  many questions about  uh debt about personal loans about how  to get money from a bank i thought i'd  give a little bit of an overview of the  different types of loans available  uh if you've got questions feel free to  comment them below and i'll do my best  to answer if you found this video  helpful smash the like button subscribe  i usually do property investment videos  on this channel and i do a video every  single day so do subscribe  and i look forward to seeing you on the  next video tomorrow thanks so much peace  [Music]  you

